🏗️ Project Structure

 Routes (Next.js App Router)
```
/                    → Login page (homepage)
/register            → Registration page
/landingpage         → Marketing/landing page (not currently used)
```

 Component Architecture
```
components/
├── Beams.jsx         → 3D animated background effect
├── LoginCard.jsx     → Login form component
├── RegistrationCard.jsx → Registration form component
├── Header.jsx        → Landing page header
├── DidYouKnow.jsx    → Information section
├── WhyCommunitySystem.jsx → Features/benefits section
├── FAQ.jsx           → Frequently asked questions
├── Footer.jsx        → Footer component
└── SplitText.jsx     → GSAP animated text component
```

---

 📦 Component Deep Dive

1. Beams.jsx (3D Background Animation)
Purpose: Creates an animated 3D beam effect using Three.js and React Three Fiber.

Key Features:
- Uses WebGL shaders for performance
- Custom noise function for organic movement
- Configurable parameters (beamWidth, beamHeight, beamNumber, speed, etc.)
- Creates a sophisticated animated background

Technical Details:
- Uses `@react-three/fiber` for React integration with Three.js
- Implements custom shader materials extending Three.js MeshStandardMaterial
- Uses 3D noise functions for beam distortion
- Renders multiple stacked planes as beams

Code Quality: 
- Well-structured but complex
- Good use of React hooks (useMemo, useRef)
- Proper cleanup in useEffect

Issues Found:
- ⚠️ ESLint disabled for React Three Fiber props (`react/no-unknown-property`)
- ⚠️ No error boundaries for WebGL failures
- ⚠️ High memory usage with many beams (30 beams × 100 segments)

---

2. LoginCard.jsx (Login Form)
Purpose: User authentication login form.

Features:
- Email/password input
- "Remember me" checkbox
- Password visibility toggle (eye icon)
- "Forgot Password?" link (non-functional)
- Google OAuth button (non-functional)
- Link to registration page

State Management:
```javascript
- email: string
- password: string
- remember: boolean
- showPassword: boolean
```

Missing Functionality:
- Form validation
- API integration
- Loading states
- Error messages
- Session management

---

3. RegistrationCard.jsx (Registration Form)
Purpose: New user registration form.

Features:
- First name / Last name fields
- Email input
- Password and confirm password
- Terms & conditions checkbox
- Google OAuth signup (non-functional)
- Link back to login

State Management:
```javascript
- firstName: string
- lastName: string
- email: string
- password: string
- confirmPassword: string
- agreeToTerms: boolean
```

---

 4. Header.jsx (Landing Page Header)
Purpose: Hero section for marketing/landing page.

Features:
- Large headline: "Report with Ease, Track with Confidence"
- Subtitle: "Welcome to Marias Heights Community System"
- "Learn More" CTA button linking to #features


 5. DidYouKnow.jsx (Information Section)
Purpose: Displays community information.

Content: Basic placeholder text about Marias Heights serving for 10 years.


 6. WhyCommunitySystem.jsx (Features Section)
Purpose: Shows value propositions (Vision, Mission, Values).

Features:
- 3-column grid layout
- Orange-themed cards
- Responsive design

 7. FAQ.jsx (Frequently Asked Questions)
Purpose: Displays common questions.

 8. Footer.jsx (Footer)
Purpose: Site footer with copyright.

 9. SplitText.jsx (GSAP Animation Component)
Purpose: Animated text component using GSAP SplitText plugin.

Features:
- Scroll-triggered animations
- Character/word/line splitting
- Configurable animation parameters
- Font loading detection


 🔄 Route Analysis

 `/` (app/page.jsx) - Login Page
- Current State: Login page with Beams background
- Components Used: Beams, LoginCard
- Status: ✅ Functional UI, ❌ No backend

 `/register` (app/register/page.jsx) - Registration Page
- Current State: Registration form with Beams background
- Components Used: Beams, RegistrationCard
- Status: ✅ Functional UI, ❌ No backend, ❌ Spacing issues

 `/landingpage` (app/landingpage/page.jsx) - Marketing Page
- Current State: Landing page with Header, DidYouKnow, WhyCommunitySystem, FAQ, Footer
- Components Used: Header, DidYouKnow, WhyCommunitySystem, FAQ, Footer
- Status: ✅ Basic structure, ⚠️ Needs content enhancement
- Note: This route exists but may not be the main entry point



